# AI.md is OS layer rather than project state: it is the Session Closing
# Ritual, the canon /mv-close is required to read instead of restating. Its
# neighbour Current Context records this project's situation and does not
# travel.
#
# Findings.md is deliberately NOT listed, though it is equally structural. An
# index carries entries, and entries are instances: shipping this project's
# would give upstream twenty-one broken links to Findings it does not have.
# Its shape belongs in Templates/ if it is ever to travel. Noticed when a
# delivery carried it and upstream's validator rejected the result.
Project-OS/06-AI/AI.md

# Docs/ is the developer documentation of the OS itself: how every part works
# and why. It describes the layer, not this project, so it travels with it. Its
# pages may link only to paths this manifest covers (or to Docs/ itself) —
# upstream has none of this project's Tasks or Findings.
Docs/**

# `.claude/` is deliberately absent from this list, and cannot be in it.
# Every path here is relative to the vault, and the project-root `.claude/` is
# outside the vault by construction — so the two lines that used to sit here
# (`.claude/commands/**`, `.claude/hooks/**`) declared a delivery the transport
# could never perform. Upstream had no `.claude/` at all for weeks, and nothing
# reported it, because a manifest line for a file that does not exist under the
# vault matches nothing.
#
# The sources now live in `Knowledge-OS/Dist/` and travel from there.
# `Knowledge-OS/Tools/adopt.mjs` materializes them into whatever project root
# the OS is installed into, and `deployed-command-drift` fails the validator
# if the deployed copy and its source ever disagree.

# Per-copy files: part of the system, but every copy keeps its own, so they
# are deliberately absent too. A manifest line is a promise that
# `upgrade.mjs` may overwrite the path in any project the OS is installed
# into, and these would overwrite that project's README, its Obsidian
# settings, its own OS backlog:
#
#   CLAUDE.md  README.md  .os-version
#   .obsidian/app.json  .obsidian/templates.json
#   Backlog.md
#
# Toward upstream they are carried by hand, as a step of /mv-sync. Before
# that step existed, the `Docs/` line added to CLAUDE.md here never reached
# upstream, and nothing reported it. Backlog-Archive.md is not among them: it
# is this project's record of how OS entries were closed, and stays here.
# PER_COPY_FILES in Tools/manifest.mjs is this list in a form code reads.

# Installation state is absent for another reason: `.mvos/install.json`, which
# adopt.mjs writes on every apply (project root, mode, deployed files with
# their hashes), and `.mvos/os-base.json`, which upgrade.mjs writes on every
# upgrade (the hashes of the version taken: the next upgrade's base), describe
# one installation and mean nothing anywhere else. They never travel, not even
# by hand, are not in PER_COPY_FILES, and upgrade.mjs never touches them. Nor does
# `mvos.config.json`, the project's own settings (its language, the language
# of its notes): the OS layer names no language, and each project names its
# own, with adopt.mjs --language or by hand.
